==== exit ====
0
==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael server serve [--config <path>] [--host <address>] [--port <n>] [--database <path>]

Run a Raphael server on this machine.

The API key comes from RAPHAEL_SERVER_API_KEY, in the environment or in a .env
file. With --config, .env is read from that file's directory; without it, from
the current directory.

Make an owner-only key file with:
`[ -e .env ] && echo ".env already exists; add RAPHAEL_SERVER_API_KEY to it yourself." >&2 || (umask 077 && set -C && echo "RAPHAEL_SERVER_API_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" > .env)`.
Clients log in with the same key. It must be 1 to 512 visible ASCII characters
with no spaces. In .env, quote a key that contains #, which otherwise starts a
comment.

Clients read RAPHAEL_API_KEY, not RAPHAEL_SERVER_API_KEY, so starting a server
never changes which server client commands use.

Without --config, listens on 127.0.0.1:3000 with the database at
./data/raphael.sqlite, relative to the current directory.

The YAML file may set server.host, server.port and database.path; every key is
optional and unknown keys are refused. A relative database.path resolves against
the file's directory.

Flags override the file. A relative --database resolves against the current
directory.

The port is bound before the database is opened, so a port in use creates
nothing.

This command never reads your saved login. It prints only to standard error and
runs until Ctrl-C.

A stop by signal finishes the shutdown, then exits 130 after Ctrl-C (SIGINT) or
143 after SIGTERM. A second signal stops it at once, without finishing.

Options:
      --config <path>
          Read configuration from this YAML file.
      --host <address>
          Address to listen on. 0.0.0.0 listens on every interface. Default:
          127.0.0.1.
      --port <n>
          Port to listen on, from 1 to 65535. Default: 3000.
      --database <path>
          SQLite database file. Created if it does not exist. Default:
          ./data/raphael.sqlite.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael server serve
  raphael server serve --port 3100
  raphael server serve --config ./raphael.yaml
  raphael server serve --host 0.0.0.0 --database ./data/raphael.sqlite

Prints:
  The address, the database, where the key came from, and the login command, on
  standard error. Standard output is empty.

Next: raphael login http://127.0.0.1:3000

See also: raphael help connecting
